  "_": "Drink photo per drink, keyed by the Hebrew name in drinks.json. Source: Canva folder FAHUB4yCGHI (10 family subfolders, 48 designs, one per drink), mapped 2026-09-02 by matching each Canva design title to the drink; all 48 matched unambiguously. Each was exported from Canva as a transparent PNG, trimmed to its alpha bounding box at alpha>=160 — a threshold picked by sweeping 16/48/96/160/220 across all 48 and taking the plateau: below it the box swells to include the soft drop shadow (up to 49% larger on five shots, which shrank the glass and left a grey rectangle on the card), above it the glass itself starts to erode, scaled to a uniform 520px height so every glass renders the same size on the card, and encoded as WebP. One export — DAHUB_z-lP0 — came back on an opaque white card rather than cut out; its background was removed by a border-seeded flood fill of near-white, which leaves interior whites (foam) intact. Uploaded to Shopify Files via stagedUploadsCreate + fileCreate, so the pages reference cdn.shopify.com and the theme carries no image weight. 'canva' is the design id: re-export from it if a photo has to be regenerated. 'w' is the delivered pixel width at height 520 — it is the <img width> attribute, so the browser reserves the right box and the grid does not shift while the photo loads.",
